{
  "ideas": [
    {
      "id": 26,
      "name": "Aim the Cannon",
      "approach": "handmade",
      "approachWhy": "Each layout is a few cannons and islands, and its feel comes from how the swing and the target line up (pause at the ends, a moving island, a wall with a sliding hole, a cracking seat). A generator would mostly roll the same layouts with other numbers, so 18 hand-made ones, each checked for a fair fire window, work better.",
      "engine": {
        "have": [
          "\"cannon\" look and ObbyCourse.CANNON = 75 launch speed (SlimeCannon section)",
          "slide motion (islands that drift left-right or up-down)",
          "shrink motion (an island that breathes bigger and smaller)",
          "swing motion (pendulum) and spin motion, as a base for the barrel's sweep",
          "fall = back to the start pad; red see-through hazard look",
          "tests that check every gap against the jump and launch limits",
          "idea 4 Bounce Chain gave up its cannon variants, so every cannon in the course is an aimed one from this idea"
        ],
        "new": [
          {
            "what": "Cannon seat controller on the client: walk into the barrel's mouth, the character snaps in, the camera sits behind the barrel, jump fires. No walking out and no auto-fire.",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "Scripted flight: the shot follows a fixed arc for the aim at the moment you fire (same arc every time), then hands the character back to normal physics just above the landing spot. A miss ends over the void or in red goo, which uses the shared 'hazard touch = back to the start pad' from idea 1.",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "New motion kind \"aim\": the barrel sweeps its yaw (left-right) between two angles, with an optional short pause at each end (eased like the 'shuttle' slide of ideas 3 and 25: hold, move, hold). Pitch nod for Two Axes runs as a second motion on the same part through the 'two motions on one part' system ideas 9 and 15 plan ('Wobble'), not a separate one.",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Aim line visuals: a dotted line from the barrel that follows the real arc and ends in a landing dot; it turns red when the arc would hit goo; a target ring on each island lights green while the dot is inside it.",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Test helper: compute the fire window per sweep (time the landing dot sits inside a safe island and the arc misses all goo) and fail if it is under the tier minimum (easy 0.8 s, medium 0.45 s, hard 0.3 s). The arc itself goes through the shared 'launch reach' check (idea 4's launchReaches(), shared with ideas 6, 16, 21); moving islands and the sliding wall hole use idea 3's moving-part gap check.",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "Catch cannon: a cannon with a wide funnel mouth that grabs you out of the air and starts swinging at once (for cannon-to-cannon variants).",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Hot Seat: the cannon's deck cracks and darkens once you sit in it and drops you 3 s later; start it with the shared one-shot stand-on trigger (ideas 3, 21, 24) and the crack look from idea 2's melt, not new code.",
            "size": "S"
          }
        ]
      },
      "readability": "A fat goo cannon on a turntable with a dotted aim line running out of the barrel to a landing dot; every safe island wears a big target ring that glows green while the dot is on it. A click-click tick plays as the barrel sweeps and a deep thump when it fires.",
      "generator": null,
